  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115640",
      "title": "Accessing Host Elements Programmatically",
      "lectureOrder": 118,
      "videoOrder": 112,
      "sourceHash": "1cf83c0e9fcc9d3190726e9e590a1c3307e30b00e4898ca6faa74847ac3236f0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "So knowing how to listen to events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 6.717,
          "en": "on the host element and knowing about HostBinding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.717,
          "end": 11.127,
          "en": "and HostListener is important as an Angular developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 17,
          "en": "There is one other last host element-related feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "you should know about though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "because sometimes in certain situations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 27.41,
          "en": "you might need programmatic access to the host element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "So you might need to interact with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "from inside your TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 35.82,
          "en": "For example, let's say here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.82,
          "end": 37.98,
          "en": "when we click on the host element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.98,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "I wanna output some information about it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "which obviously is not a real use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "But here in this app I don't have a real use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "because it is a feature you won't need that often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 51.99,
          "en": "but you should still know about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.99,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "So for this demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "let's say we wanna log some host element information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "whenever it is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "Now, what you can do to achieve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 67.82,
          "en": "is you can inject a special value into your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 72.39,
          "en": "a value that will be provided by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.39,
          "end": 75.63,
          "en": "and you can inject either with the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 78.18,
          "en": "as you learned it for services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "or with help of that inject function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "about which you also learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.17,
          "end": 86.46000000000001,
          "en": "And I'll use the latter here, but both would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.46000000000001,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "So for that, I'll add a private property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "which therefore won't be exposed to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 95.343,
          "en": "of this component since I don't need access to it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.11,
          "en": "And I'll name it el, but the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.11,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "And the value of that property should then be the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 105.813,
          "en": "of calling inject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 110.913,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 114.18,
          "en": "And to inject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 118.65,
          "en": "we now have to pass a special class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "the ElementRef class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 125.343,
          "en": "which also must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.736,
          "end": 131.43,
          "en": "ElementRef is a class defined by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.43,
          "end": 134.43,
          "en": "So it's part of the Angular framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.43,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "which defines a reference to some element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "that's rendered to the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "So it's pretty generic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "because it can refer to any element on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "But by injecting it into a component like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "Angular will give you access to the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 153.633,
          "en": "of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 157.317,
          "en": "So therefore here, we can console.log(this.el).",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 163.95,
          "en": "And with that, if you save it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.95,
          "end": 168.95,
          "en": "and you reload, if you click on that app-control element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 171.39,
          "en": "you get clicked, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 175.473,
          "en": "but you also get that injected ElementRef object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "and that is then an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "that has a nativeElement property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 186.26,
          "en": "And that property then actually holds your host element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.16,
          "en": "So if I expand that, you see that this is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.16,
          "end": 194.64,
          "en": "what Angular knows about the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.64,
          "end": 196.263,
          "en": "that's rendered to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.1,
          "end": 200.16,
          "en": "And it's essentially a collection of properties that exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.16,
          "end": 202.623,
          "en": "for all DOM elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "And you could now extract information from those properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "You could also change them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "though you should be careful about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 216.09,
          "en": "because you typically don't wanna start changing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.09,
          "end": 219.3,
          "en": "what's visible on the page programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.3,
          "end": 221.7,
          "en": "by using the ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.7,
          "end": 225.78,
          "en": "Instead, you should change what's visible on the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.78,
          "end": 229.35,
          "en": "by changing data and using template features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.35,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "as we always did it throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 236.76,
          "en": "But if you need programmatic access to the host element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.76,
          "end": 241.383,
          "en": "this is how you can get it: by injecting ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
